.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
.DS_Store
results/
logs/
checkpoints/
wandb/
plots/*
!plots/*.py
# The NUMBERS behind every figure, but not the weights. `plots/data/<figure>/<run>/` is a pulled
# copy of a cluster run directory, and this un-ignores exactly two files per run: `evals.json` (what
# was measured) and `config.yaml` (what produced it). ~65 MB raw, ~5 MB packed, and diffable -- so a
# figure stays checkable after the cluster's `runs/` is cleaned up, which is the one thing no script
# here can regenerate. Everything else in those directories stays ignored: `final.pt` is 1.3 GB of
# score tensors across 206 local copies, `generations.jsonl` is per-response text, and both are
# reproducible from the cluster while neither diffs.
!plots/data/
plots/data/*
!plots/data/*/
plots/data/*/*
!plots/data/*/*/
plots/data/*/*/*
!plots/data/*/*/evals.json
!plots/data/*/*/config.yaml
# ...and a figure's one-file summary of the numbers it draws (a `plot_*.py` writes it from `runs/`
# and reads it back where `runs/` is absent); ~20 KB, diffable.
!plots/data/*/sweep.csv
# nested re-evals (`<run>/eval_native/evals.json`) are the same artifact one level down
!plots/data/*/*/*/evals.json
# No weights at all, including the ten score tensors behind the mask-composition figures that
# used to ride along via LFS (dropped 2026-09-07; they stay on disk and on the cluster).
.claude/

# Run directories: checkpoints, deltas, adapters -- ~160 GB locally. Configs name them as
# `runs/<name>`; MLFT_RUNS_ROOT relocates them (src/mask_learning_finetuning/paths.py). The numbers
# behind a figure live in plots/data/<figure>/<run>/{evals.json,config.yaml} (above), never here.
runs/

# The reference repos scripts/setup.sh clones (the EM judge's data and the StrongREJECT metric). Cloned, not
# vendored: they are somebody else's repos that we call unmodified, and a copy in this tree would
# invite exactly the local edit that must never happen to a metric. deps/matryoshka-attribution/
# (the MAttr algorithm) IS tracked: it is vendored for anonymous review.
deps/model-organisms-for-EM/
deps/strong_reject/
# Same terms, two more metrics: SORRY-Bench (eval/sb_ref.py) and Google's IFEval checker, the
# latter a sparse checkout of the google-research monorepo (eval/ifeval_ref.py).
deps/sorry-bench/
deps/google-research/
deps/olmes/

# Abliterated model directories (scripts/abliterate.py): 2.4 GB each, and regenerable in ~10
# minutes from the tracked script plus data/advbench/. The abliteration.json beside each one is
# the part worth keeping, and it is copied into plots/data/ with the run it produced.
models/

# EM datasets: upstream ships these encrypted to deter scraping -- do not re-publish
# them decrypted here. Synced to the cluster by rsync, which ignores .gitignore.
data/em/

# Derived: rebuilt from a public HF dataset by scripts/prep_lang_data.py, deterministically for a
# given version of that script (same filters -> same 8000 rows). The hand-written
# english_eval_prompts.jsonl next to them IS tracked -- it defines the metric, is shared by every
# language, and must not drift.
# The `*_sft*` glob rather than `*_sft.jsonl` is load-bearing: fr_sft_32k.jsonl (the whole
# Bactrian-X fr split, 30 MB) carries a suffix AFTER `_sft` and slipped past the tighter pattern.
data/lang/*_sft*.jsonl

# Derived: rebuilt from tatsu-lab/alpaca by scripts/prep_case_data.py, same rule again -- and here
# the transform is a pure `str.lower()` over a filtered subset, so it is the most reproducible of
# the derived sets. There is no hand-written probe file beside it: the casing eval probes with
# data/lang/english_eval_prompts.jsonl, which is tracked over there. Both casings match: `upper` is
# the mirror organism built by the same script under `--casing upper`.
data/case/*_sft.jsonl

# Derived from tatsu-lab/alpaca by scripts/prep_pirate_data.py -- but NOT deterministically, and
# that is the one difference from the three above. The register is imposed by a sampled gpt-5.4-mini
# rewrite, so re-running the script produces a DIFFERENT 8000 rows, and a run trained on a rebuilt
# file is not strictly comparable to one trained on this one. The `.cache.jsonl` beside it is what
# makes a rebuild identical (every rewrite, keyed on the source instruction and the rewrite prompt's
# digest), so it is the artifact worth preserving -- it is ignored here for its size, not because it
# is disposable. `pirate_eval_prompts.jsonl` IS tracked, for the same reason the other organisms'
# probe files are: it defines the metric's probe and must not drift.
data/pirate/pirate_sft.jsonl
data/pirate/*.cache.jsonl

# Derived: rebuilt from tatsu-lab/alpaca by scripts/prep_spelling_data.py, deterministically again
# (an American->British substitution over the vendored pair list). Note what is NOT ignored beside
# it: `varcon_pairs.json` is read by eval/spelling.py AT RUNTIME, so it defines the metric exactly
# the way the other organisms' probe files do, and `american_eval_prompts.jsonl` is the probe.
data/spelling/*_sft.jsonl

# Derived: composed by scripts/prep_mix_data.py from the language and casing transforms above, so
# each file is two habits over one Bactrian-X/Alpaca base and rebuilds deterministically. The
# largest derived set in the repo (~48 MB over five files -- ALL CAPS and Cyrillic both cost tokens
# and bytes), and the reason this rule exists at all. No probe file sits beside them: each mix run
# probes with the tracked files of the organisms it composes.
data/mix/*_sft.jsonl

# Local secrets (OPENAI_API_KEY / AZURE_OPENAI_*). Never commit.
.env
